load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# A deductive system: a set of axioms and inference rules for deriving theorems, the formal engine of proof. A
# derivation is a chain of rule applications from axioms to a conclusion. The kernel's type checker is a deductive
# system whose theorems are well-typed terms. The form carries the set of formulas; the axioms and inference rules are
# the system.
form deductive-system
  link formulas, like set
